#note: See @bib{RN117@209}: “The verb @i{warādum} is the standard verb for entering a forest in Gilgameš, even when the forest in question is known to be situated, like the Cedar Forest, on uplands (OB Ishchali 37': @i{ūridma irtahiṣ qištam}, SB II 224 // 281 // 295: @i{mannu ša urradu ana qištīšu}, II 229 // 286 // 294: @i{ārid qištšu}). Neither dictionary accepts J. V. Kinnier Wilson’s bold contention that @i{warādum} can refer to upward motion as well as downward (in Garelli, Gilg., p. 106, fn. 1).” @bib{RN2651@10b}: “Jn fact, @i{warādum}, besides designating spatial descent, carries also the meaning of advancing, in any direction, with inimical intention.”
